@format 1
@id relay.deliver-output
@title Deliver completed output
@area 6. Relay and routing
@entry input
@summary Resume plan-owned output from durable stage snapshots, while retaining compatible live-tab delivery for legacy work.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.complete, queue.clear-tabs, relay.receive-tab
@tag relay
@tag delivery

@alias courier = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LCourier
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias surface = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PTabSurface
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias planstore = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LRelayPlanStore

[input] Schedule change after completion <input>
- Scan done targeted work that has not already been delivered @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
- Accept work owned by this process, or saved-plan work whose recorded owner is no longer alive @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
> reserve

[reserve] Reserve this delivery attempt <process>
- Add the work ID to the delivered set before attempting delivery @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
> target

[target] Resolve delivery target <decision>
? "Finish target" > finish
? "Output file is missing" > retry
? "Output file exists" > route-kind

[route-kind] Select saved or live destination <decision>
- Look for the work's stable target in its saved batch plan @ planstore.LRelayPlanRead(...)
? "Stable stage exists in the saved batch plan" > plan
? "Live destination tab and list are available" > add
? "No usable saved or live destination exists" > retry

[plan] Resolve saved delivery <decision>
- Load the saved batch plan and resolve the work's stable target stage @ planstore.LRelayPlanRead(...)
- Check whether this work ID was already committed to the plan @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
? "Work was already committed" > plan-drain
? "Work has not been committed" > plan-apply

[plan-apply] Apply and persist saved stage <process>
- Append the stage input and execute, route, collect, or pause it according to the saved stage snapshot @ courier.LCourierStageArrive(...)
- Record the delivered work ID and save the mutated plan @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
> plan-save

[plan-save] Was plan delivery committed? <decision>
- Inspect the final durable-plan save result @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
? "Plan save succeeds" > plan-drain
? "Plan save fails" > retry

[plan-drain] Drain saved-plan source <process>
- Apply ordinary preference-based source cleanup without invoking the live-tab arrival path @ courier.LCourierSourceRemove(...)
> plan-result

[finish] Finish relay chain <process>
- Record chain completion and force source removal @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
> finish-remove

[finish-remove] Force source cleanup <process>
- Remove source list and group paths regardless of the relay-empty preference @ courier.LCourierSourceRemove(...)
> finished

[add] Add output to destination <process>
- Add the output path to the destination list with its batch cohort @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
> accepted

[accepted] Did the destination accept the output? <decision>
- Accept either a newly added path or the same path already present in the destination @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
? "New or already present" > drain
? "Destination rejected the path" > retry

[drain] Should source inputs be removed? <decision>
- Apply the force flag and relay-empty preference, then resolve a stable plan-stage source back to its original live tab when available @ courier.LCourierTabFind(...)
@ courier.LCourierSourceRemove(...)
? "Source removal is disabled or impossible" > arrive
? "Source removal proceeds" > remove

[remove] Remove source containers <process>
- Remove the delivered source and merge-source paths from the source list @ list.PListPathsRemove(...)
- Remove matching paths from the source group container @ group.PGroupPathsRemove(...)
- When a removed path is loaded, force-close its viewer and directly clear its flow @ surface.PTabViewerAttach(...)
@ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
@ flow.PFlowClear(...)
> arrive

[arrive] Continue downstream relay <process>
- Invoke automatic downstream action when enabled @ courier.LCourierArrive(...)
> result

[retry] Delivery not committed <error>
- Remove the reserved work ID when delivery returns false, or remove it and rethrow when delivery raises @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
= The completed work remains eligible for a later delivery attempt; source content is not drained.

[result] Delivery complete <output>
= The destination accepted the output before source removal; any removed loaded media and its dependent flow state are cleared even in an inactive source tab.

[plan-result] Saved-plan delivery complete <output>
= The saved stage accepted and persisted the output before source removal; continuation was governed by the stage snapshot rather than live-tab arrival.

[finished] Relay chain finished <output>
= Source paths are drained without delivery to another tab, and the work ID remains marked delivered.
